{"id": "EUVD-2026-32475", "enisaUuid": "bba92fed-9b7c-3f0a-8e95-d8b679552227", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtw88: check for PCI upstream bridge existence\n\npci_upstream_bridge() returns NULL if the device is on a root bus.  If\n8821CE is installed in the system with such a PCI topology, the probing\nroutine will crash.  This has probably been unnoticed as 8821CE is mostly\nsupplied in laptops where there is a PCI-to-PCI bridge located upstream\nfrom the device.  However the card might be installed on a system with\ndifferent configuration.\n\nCheck if the bridge does exist for the specific workaround to be applied.\n\nFound by Linux Verification Center (linuxtesting.org) with Svace static\nanalysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:58:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:20:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/959c13da6c36167ce1016d400a6104d2367f686e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b89b4c095804c478d50376285e66700cf3c045f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc9b6303e7ea91bc360b42c7edc1fe9ceb2f47fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c53d68e3bcfc8faccdd76c3383a9232b05c9ae6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/000134a20bbf89b1152520a2eef71f91fdb83a5b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bbbb56204f7359ce2139a9341b43b52a186261c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb101d2abdcccb514ca4fccd3b278dd8267374f6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wxwq-c95x-686r", "CVE-2026-46092"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2dbe1acc-a0e2-3672-b9ad-3583d3b2e24b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "41bc7351-d3a2-3456-ab67-e94eb2f96b44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "24f5e38a13b5ae2b6105cda8bb47c19108e62a9a <3bbbb56204f7359ce2139a9341b43b52a186261c"}, {"id": "443a899f-95ea-3813-84f5-8154d43a7e9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_v